# Generated data and research output. PROTOCOL.md has said "Never commit generated data. Never
# `git add -A`" since campaign 1; until now that was enforced by discipline alone, and 46 GB sat
# one stray `git add -A` away from the pack -- where it could not be removed without rewriting
# history. Nothing under these paths has ever been tracked, so ignoring them takes nothing away.
#
# This matters more since campaign-2 FOM output was taken OUT of git-lfs (.gitattributes, and
# DWMM's call of 2026-08-27): a large file that is not an lfs pointer is a large file in the pack.
# The two changes belong together.
#
# The scripts that regenerate all of this ARE committed; that is what makes the data disposable.
